samirctl-mint -- real dBASE III PLUS 1.1 program-control transcripts
(bead initech-39e5; audit 2026-10-23-samir L002 L003 L013 L022 L041).

What: the *.PRG programs real DBASE.EXE 1.1 ran and the *.TXT files it
wrote with SET ALTERNATE (CR LF, closing ^Z). They are the goldens of
test-samir-ctl (harness/diff/dbf_diff/test_samir_ctl.c); samirctl_mint.md5
pins them and the Makefile checks it before every replay. Nothing here is
generated by SAMIR.

  ESC      Esc in DO WHILE .T.: Ignore, Esc, Cancel  -> *** INTERRUPTED *** ...
  ESCS     Esc, Suspend, RESUME, Esc, Cancel         -> Do suspended ...
  ESCTRAP  ON ESCAPE STOP=.T. ends the loop          -> TRAPPED .T.
  NEST     recursive procedure + ON ERROR            -> TRAP 19 103 DOs nested too deep.
  RAW      the same with no trap                     -> 19 RAWP + 1 RAW "Called from"
  MASTER   RETURN TO MASTER two levels down          -> MASTER FIRST SECOND MASTER RESUMED
  QUITP    QUIT inside a program                     -> BEFORE QUIT only
  RETRYM   RETRY from the ON ERROR handler ERH.PRG   -> 7 / DONE 1

How (2026-10-23): dosbox-x 2024.03.01, SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy, machine
svga_s3, 386, 8 MB, DATE 07/24/1986; C: = a working directory holding
DBASE.EXE, DBASEINL.OVL, DBASE.MSG (disk 1) and DBASE.OVL (disk 2) of
$DBASE3_DECOMP/goldens/dbase-iii-plus-1.1/extracted, plus CONFIG.DB
(STATUS/BELL/SAFETY/TALK OFF). Keystrokes are typed by the program itself:
"RUN AUTOTYPE -w 0 -p 0.1 esc i esc c ..." queues them in the BIOS buffer,
then dBASE reads them (AUTOTYPE in the autoexec runs before DBASE starts
and the keys are lost). Procedures live in SET PROCEDURE files or separate
program files: III+ 1.1 keeps them out of the main program file.

  DBASE3_DECOMP=../dbase3-decomp python3 -I mint_setup.py
  DBASE3_DECOMP=... python3 -I mint_run.py esc        (nest raw esc escs
                                     esctrap master quitp retry)

mint_setup.py writes the programs and confs into the working directory
($SAMIRCTL_MINT_DIR, default $DBASE3_DECOMP/mint/samirctl); mint_run.py
runs one case (timeout -k 5; dosbox-x ignores SIGTERM) and prints the
transcript plus a dump of the 80x25 text page made by SCRDUMP.COM
(scrdump.asm, nasm -f bin). Copy the PRG/TXT files back here and refresh
samirctl_mint.md5 only as a deliberate act.
